---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';

// TODO before publishing: confirm the legal entity name, mailing address and the
// contact address below with counsel. Everything else describes what the product
// actually does today.
const ENTITY = 'venOS';
const CONTACT = 'hello@venos.app';
const UPDATED = 'September 1, 2026';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — venOS"
  description="How venOS collects, uses and protects your data."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated={UPDATED}
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what {ENTITY} collects when you use our website and the venOS
    application, why we collect it, and what control you have over it. It applies to
    venview.io and to the venOS app.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {ENTITY} provides software that helps food and beverage vendors understand the
    profitability of the events they work. You can reach us at
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>

  <h3>Information you give us</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account details</strong> — your email address and password. Passwords are hashed by our authentication provider; we never see or store them in readable form.</li>
    <li><strong>Company and event information</strong> — company name, contact details, and the events, venues, recipes, inventory, supplies, expenses and staffing you enter.</li>
    <li><strong>Correspondence</strong> — messages you send us, including support requests and waitlist signups.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Information from services you connect</h3>
  <p>
    If you connect a point-of-sale system such as Square, we retrieve the data needed to
    calculate your event profit. That includes completed order and payment totals,
    processing fees, refunds, discounts, tips, applied sales taxes, item and modifier
    catalogs, business locations, and timecards with the associated wage rates and staff
    names. We request read-only access and never initiate charges or modify anything in
    your POS account.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can disconnect a point-of-sale integration at any time from Settings, which
    revokes our access.
  </p>

  <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Usage analytics</strong> — pages viewed, features used, approximate location derived from IP address, browser and device type.</li>
    <li><strong>Log data</strong> — technical records generated when the application runs, used to diagnose errors and abuse.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide the service — calculating event profit, costs, labor and tax figures from the data you and your connected systems supply.</li>
    <li>To operate your account, including authentication and billing.</li>
    <li>To send transactional email such as confirmations, password resets and notifications about your account.</li>
    <li>To improve the product by understanding which features are used and where people encounter problems.</li>
    <li>To protect the service against fraud, abuse and security incidents.</li>
    <li>To meet legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use your business or sales
    data to train machine learning models for other customers.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    We share data only with service providers that make the product work, and only to the
    extent each needs to do its job:
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Supabase</td><td>Database hosting and user authentication</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Fly.io</td><td>Application hosting</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Square</td><td>Point-of-sale integration, when you connect one</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Stripe</td><td>Subscription billing and payment processing</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Resend</td><td>Transactional email delivery</td></tr>
      <tr><td>PostHog, Google Analytics, Contentsquare</td><td>Product and website analytics</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Anthropic</td><td>AI features such as recipe import and cost mapping suggestions</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    We may also disclose information if required by law, or in connection with a merger or
    acquisition — in which case we will give you notice before your data becomes subject
    to a different policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Payments</h2>
  <p>
    Subscription payments are processed by Stripe. Card numbers are submitted directly to
    Stripe and never reach our servers. We retain only the subscription status and billing
    metadata needed to run your account.
  </p>

  <h2>How we protect it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Data is encrypted in transit using TLS.</li>
    <li>Point-of-sale access tokens are encrypted at rest using AES-256-GCM before being stored.</li>
    <li>Access to company data is restricted to members of that company, enforced at the database level.</li>
    <li>Access to production systems is limited to personnel who need it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    No system is perfectly secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security. If we become
    aware of a breach affecting your personal information, we will notify you as required
    by applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep your account and business data for as long as your account is active. If you
    delete your company or close your account, we delete the associated data, except where
    we are required to retain records — for example billing history for tax and accounting
    purposes. Backups and system logs are retained on a rolling basis and expire in the
    ordinary course.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, export or
    delete your personal information, to object to or restrict certain processing, and to
    withdraw consent. Residents of California may request disclosure of the categories of
    personal information collected and may opt out of any sale or sharing of personal
    information — we do not sell personal information. Residents of the European Economic
    Area and the United Kingdom have corresponding rights under the GDPR.
  </p>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>. We will
    not discriminate against you for making a request.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
  <p>
    We use cookies and similar technologies to keep you signed in, remember preferences,
    and understand how the product is used. You can block cookies in your browser, though
    parts of the application will not work without them. We honor Global Privacy Control
    signals where required.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    venOS is a business tool and is not directed at children. We do not knowingly collect
    personal information from anyone under 16.
  </p>

  <h2>International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Our service providers may process data in the United States and other countries. Where
    data is transferred out of the EEA or UK, we rely on appropriate safeguards such as
    standard contractual clauses.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy as the product changes. We will update the date at the top,
    and for material changes we will give notice through the application or by email.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy or your data: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
